cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Rank3KUM: A Lean 4 formalization of the divisible case of the rank-three Kajitani-Ueno-Miyano cyclic basis ordering theorem"
abstract: >-
  A complete, machine-checked Lean 4 formalization of the divisible case of the
  rank-three Kajitani-Ueno-Miyano conjecture: every finite uniformly dense matroid
  of rank three whose ground set has cardinality divisible by three admits a cyclic
  basis ordering, that is, a cyclic ordering of its ground set in which every three
  cyclically consecutive elements form a basis. No restriction to representable,
  paving, simple, graphic or small matroids is imposed; matroids with nontrivial
  parallel classes are covered. The development contains no `sorry`, `admit`,
  `axiom`, `unsafe` declaration, or use of `native_decide`, and the main theorem
  depends only on the standard Mathlib axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice` and
  `Quot.sound`.
type: software
authors:
